# Story 46: Voice Prompting (Ctrl+R) (45s)
# Hook: Talk to your terminal. Press Ctrl+R, speak your prompt, and Rysh transcribes it for you.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-046-voice-prompting.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Talk to your terminal. Press Ctrl+R, speak your prompt, and Rysh transcribes it for you.

[00:03.0 --> 00:12.0]
Voice prompting starts in your config. Under the voice section, set enabled to true. The default hotkey is Ctrl+R.

[00:12.0 --> 00:20.0]
With voice enabled, launch rysh as usual. You're in normal mode -- ready to dictate into the active pane.

[00:20.0 --> 00:30.0]
Press Ctrl+R to start recording -- the footer shows a red dot, REC, and a running timer. Speak your prompt naturally.

[00:30.0 --> 00:38.0]
Press Ctrl+R again to stop. Rysh shows 'transcribing', then drops the text into the input field. Review it, then press Enter to submit.

[00:38.0 --> 00:45.0]
Because voice just fills the input field, it works everywhere typing does -- even when you're controlling a remote shared pane.

